1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,355
McDonald's sells BILLIONS of burgers.

2
00:00:02,705 --> 00:00:03,993
But a HUGE share of its money

3
00:00:03,993 --> 00:00:05,415
comes from something ELSE.

4
00:00:05,765 --> 00:00:06,682
REAL ESTATE.

5
00:00:07,582 --> 00:00:10,475
About 95% of its restaurants

6
00:00:10,475 --> 00:00:11,748
are run by FRANCHISEES,

7
00:00:11,748 --> 00:00:13,619
independent owners like SAM.

8
00:00:13,969 --> 00:00:15,970
Sam runs the kitchen, hires the staff,

9
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:17,361
and flips the BURGERS.

10
00:00:18,261 --> 00:00:19,349
But here's the TWIST.

11
00:00:19,699 --> 00:00:21,562
McDonald's often OWNS the building,

12
00:00:21,562 --> 00:00:23,219
and much of the LAND under it.

13
00:00:23,569 --> 00:00:25,057
So every MONTH,

14
00:00:25,057 --> 00:00:26,044
Sam pays McDonald's RENT.

15
00:00:26,944 --> 00:00:28,671
Rent is usually a SLICE of sales,

16
00:00:28,671 --> 00:00:29,589
with a MINIMUM.

17
00:00:29,939 --> 00:00:31,603
Plus a ROYALTY on every sale.

18
00:00:31,953 --> 00:00:36,735
In 2024, franchise RENT brought in about $10 BILLION,

19
00:00:36,735 --> 00:00:38,311
almost DOUBLE the royalties.

20
00:00:39,211 --> 00:00:40,939
Burger sales can have a BAD year.

21
00:00:41,289 --> 00:00:42,550
But the rent keeps COMING,

22
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:45,001
and busy corners can RISE in value.

23
00:00:45,901 --> 00:00:47,565
So it's not JUST selling burgers.

24
00:00:47,915 --> 00:00:50,947
As one early executive famously put it,

25
00:00:50,947 --> 00:00:52,885
they're really in the REAL ESTATE business.

26
00:00:53,235 --> 00:00:54,620
One of the BIGGEST landlords

27
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:55,347
on the PLANET.

